WEBVTT

00:04.350 --> 00:06.520
I thought I was a goner.

00:06.520 --> 00:10.740
Why did Nishida have to skip 
work without calling in?

00:10.740 --> 00:13.200
Ugh! This sucks!

00:13.200 --> 00:17.660
Thanks. Would a bonus make it up to you?

00:17.660 --> 00:18.870
A bonus?

00:18.870 --> 00:19.780
Yes.

00:20.820 --> 00:23.210
And this is on me.

00:23.210 --> 00:25.040
Thank you very much!

00:25.040 --> 00:26.620
Clarissa mixed his drink.

00:26.620 --> 00:28.130
Lucky guy.

00:28.610 --> 00:30.300
A bonus!

00:30.300 --> 00:32.520
I can buy so many photo books.

00:41.820 --> 00:44.660
Would someone swing by 
Nishida-kun's apartment for me?

00:45.060 --> 00:48.050
At least two of you, just to be safe.

02:24.380 --> 02:25.950
Man,

02:25.950 --> 02:28.660
the world's going to hell, Higuro-san.

02:28.660 --> 02:31.540
When has it not been?

02:31.540 --> 02:34.780
Why else would <i>I</i> be an 
intermediary in Shibuya?

02:37.680 --> 02:39.760
Good for you, then.

02:39.760 --> 02:42.620
It keeps getting worse, if you ask me.

02:42.620 --> 02:46.470
I can't believe Solitaire's 
been sharing legit info.

02:46.740 --> 02:49.940
I mean, some bad guy in the police

02:49.940 --> 02:53.860
had him shot at and 
hired me to do a job like this.

02:54.220 --> 02:58.240
What should I do?
 I've lost my faith in the police.

03:03.330 --> 03:05.600
My head's spinning.

03:05.600 --> 03:09.250
Shinjuku's security cameras 
show way too many people.

03:09.250 --> 03:12.630
Isn't looking for Solitaire 
a wild goose chase?

03:12.630 --> 03:15.130
If he disguises himself, we're out of luck.

03:15.130 --> 03:16.460
Pretty much.

03:16.680 --> 03:22.180
Still, knowing Solitaire, he'll return 
to the scene to watch the reaction.

03:23.210 --> 03:25.640
<i>Why did he visit this 
building in the first place?</i>

03:26.220 --> 03:30.600
<i>Did he somehow find out that Polka 
Shinoyama knows about that symbol?</i>

03:31.190 --> 03:34.690
<i>I'll need to meet Polka Shinoyama again, too.</i>

03:34.690 --> 03:37.070
Whoa! That guy's a giant!

03:37.400 --> 03:38.700
Look! Right there!

03:39.850 --> 03:42.890
Wow. He must be over two meters tall.

03:44.130 --> 03:45.910
You mean I <i>wasn't</i> seeing things?!

03:46.280 --> 03:47.520
You know him?

03:47.520 --> 03:49.620
No, the man next to him.

03:49.620 --> 03:51.680
Oh. Could he be...?

03:51.680 --> 03:55.330
Yes. Part of an organization 
I took on before.

03:55.540 --> 03:58.300
Sorry, but we're after Solitaire right now.

03:58.300 --> 04:01.130
No, I think they're related.

04:01.440 --> 04:04.760
Polka Shinoyama's friend, Takumi Kuruya,

04:04.760 --> 04:08.470
<b><i>Sanzu Sons 
(Little Devils of the River Sanzu)</i></b>

04:05.070 --> 04:08.470
belonged to a loose-knit 
gang called the Sanzu Sons.

04:08.470 --> 04:12.940
<b>Sanzu Sons (Little Devils of the River Sanzu)</b>

04:08.710 --> 04:12.940
I crushed the group, but I let 
just one of them get away.

04:12.940 --> 04:15.270
I had him pegged as their leader...

04:15.270 --> 04:17.070
A guy named Higuro.

04:19.530 --> 04:23.240
How about a donation, mister? To us.

04:23.520 --> 04:26.700
No dead body, but we've 
got ourselves a bonus.

04:27.400 --> 04:29.410
I'd like to ask you something.

04:29.410 --> 04:31.700
Shut up, you!

04:31.700 --> 04:34.420
Do you have pull?

04:34.420 --> 04:35.340
Huh?

04:35.340 --> 04:36.630
You know, pull.

04:37.110 --> 04:38.970
Contacts. Connections.

04:39.320 --> 04:43.380
As I see it, connections are love.

04:43.380 --> 04:46.590
I want to check on your love.

04:46.590 --> 04:48.610
The hell is this guy talking about?

04:48.610 --> 04:53.810
Are you related to or friends with 
any politicians or police big shots?

04:54.200 --> 04:57.210
Legendary mercenaries? Super heroes?

04:57.210 --> 05:00.270
World karate champions? Anyone like that?

05:00.480 --> 05:02.110
Even ordinary people will do.

05:02.110 --> 05:05.740
Does anyone love you enough 
to risk it all for you?

05:05.740 --> 05:07.540
Think he's high on something?

05:07.540 --> 05:09.070
Tripping balls, you mean?

05:09.070 --> 05:13.160
Then maybe the cops'll thank 
us for murdering his ass.

05:13.160 --> 05:15.640
No one like that? No one at all?

05:15.640 --> 05:17.620
No, moron!

05:17.620 --> 05:21.710
Forget that crap and start asking 
if <i>you</i> know an undertaker!

05:21.710 --> 05:24.040
Oh, I do.

05:24.040 --> 05:25.800
Illegal, of course.

05:35.730 --> 05:38.690
Do you understand why you're going to die?

05:39.000 --> 05:42.150
Is it because you got together in a place 
like this at this time of night?

05:42.930 --> 05:46.740
Because you bragged about abusing a woman?

05:47.360 --> 05:49.370
Because you picked a fight with us?

05:49.370 --> 05:50.920
No.

05:50.920 --> 05:52.880
Because you lack connections.

05:53.550 --> 05:55.350
Connections are love.

05:55.350 --> 05:58.720
And when love turns to hate, 
it's a real handful.

05:59.100 --> 06:02.790
We'd be in trouble if anyone 
dangerous cared about you.

06:02.790 --> 06:06.070
S-Shtop. We're shorry.

06:06.070 --> 06:07.760
D-Don't kill ush.

06:07.990 --> 06:12.560
You're not connected, 
so no one will save you.

06:18.650 --> 06:21.140
You sure are big on connections.

06:21.140 --> 06:23.110
It's an old story.

06:23.570 --> 06:27.930
I messed with someone, and one of their 
friends turned out to be bad news.

06:28.490 --> 06:33.120
I managed to get away, but I lost 
an organization in the process.

06:33.120 --> 06:37.660
Huh. What if those punks <i>had </i>
been well-connected, then?

06:37.660 --> 06:40.120
I'd have kept hidden a while longer.

06:41.120 --> 06:43.030
I told you the world's going to hell.

06:43.590 --> 06:47.820
Scum like you is loose 
and walking around town.

06:47.820 --> 06:50.650
As I said, it's always been this bad,

06:51.080 --> 06:53.510
but that will come to an end soon.

06:55.370 --> 06:59.940
I mean that this world is 
going to greet a new dawn.

07:00.240 --> 07:01.380
Here we are.

07:01.380 --> 07:05.350
I hope the route from five years 
ago hasn't been wrecked yet.

07:09.500 --> 07:13.370
Ugh. My head is spinning.

07:13.860 --> 07:15.930
Wait, what time is it?

07:16.310 --> 07:18.380
Where'd I put my phone?

07:19.790 --> 07:21.720
Oh, crap. It's Urai.

07:21.720 --> 07:24.720
That must mean his shift is over.

07:25.070 --> 07:27.210
Hey, Urai! Can you hear me?

07:28.220 --> 07:28.800
Huh?

07:29.670 --> 07:32.300
Huh? Umm... What?

07:35.680 --> 07:36.980
<i>I remember...</i>

07:41.730 --> 07:44.190
<b>Fortunes Told</b>

07:42.450 --> 07:44.190
Good morning!

07:44.190 --> 07:47.150
Thank you for your cooperation today!

07:47.150 --> 07:49.610
First, I'd like you to tell the fortune of...

07:51.530 --> 07:54.700
ordinary A-san here, 
who I scouted in the neighborhood!

07:54.700 --> 07:57.830
Umm... Please do what you can.

08:00.080 --> 08:02.290
We've got a familiar face.

08:02.560 --> 08:05.260
He's one of Clarissa's bartenders!

08:05.260 --> 08:06.980
What is she up to?

08:08.560 --> 08:10.750
<i>I'll start off with a jab.</i>

08:10.750 --> 08:13.710
<i>He has ties to this building's owner.</i>

08:13.710 --> 08:15.970
<i>Now, how will they react?</i>

08:15.970 --> 08:19.820
<i>I tagged along because she said I 
could make some money on the side.</i>

08:19.820 --> 08:23.640
<i>How did that turn into Polka-kun 
reading my fortune?!</i>

08:24.370 --> 08:26.360
E-Er... Hi.

08:27.670 --> 08:30.390
<i>Oh, he... doesn't recognize me.</i>

08:30.820 --> 08:32.530
<i>But Misaki-chan must, right?</i>

08:35.700 --> 08:37.700
It's nice to meet you.

08:37.700 --> 08:40.090
They haven't caught on?

08:40.650 --> 08:42.170
I'll keep my mouth shut, then.

08:42.660 --> 08:46.270
Now then, is anything troubling you?

08:46.270 --> 08:48.880
Oh, like life troubles?

08:49.120 --> 08:51.890
<i>I want to gripe about work! To really vent!</i>

08:51.890 --> 08:53.530
<i>But if it gets back to the bar...</i>

08:55.780 --> 08:57.800
<i>"Bad news" wouldn't begin to cover it!</i>

08:57.800 --> 08:59.750
L-Let me think.

08:59.750 --> 09:02.920
My shoulders have been awfully 
stiff for a little while.

09:02.920 --> 09:05.770
<i>What am I saying?! I didn't 
come here for massage therapy.</i>

09:05.770 --> 09:07.230
I imagine so.

09:08.850 --> 09:11.940
Oh, er... I know!

09:11.940 --> 09:16.220
One of my coworkers skipped his 
shift and went who knows where.

09:16.220 --> 09:20.200
Maybe you could, you know,
 divine where he is or something?

09:20.530 --> 09:24.910
Is this coworker dear to you?

09:24.910 --> 09:26.910
Huh? Well...

09:26.910 --> 09:32.730
He's not like family, but he's a friend 
I feel comfortable chatting with, so...

09:33.590 --> 09:35.380
<i>Huh? No way.</i>

09:35.380 --> 09:36.550
<i>Wait a second.</i>

09:37.470 --> 09:38.800
Fresh news.

09:38.800 --> 09:42.220
It seems like Nishida-san 
did visit this building.

09:42.220 --> 09:44.090
Nishida was here.

09:44.090 --> 09:49.940
The security cameras show him leaving 
in a hurry, wearing his uniform.

09:49.940 --> 09:53.890
So someone snatched him? What for?

09:53.890 --> 09:55.420
It makes you wonder.

09:55.420 --> 09:58.610
Yes, the timing is concerning.

09:58.610 --> 10:00.840
<b>Hands Swarm in Late-night Shinjuku?!
 A Ghostly Happening or One of Solitaire's Tricks?!</b>

09:58.990 --> 10:00.840
You think it's about Polka-kun?

10:00.840 --> 10:06.790
You mean they grabbed Nishidacchi 
to torture him for info on Polka-kun?

10:06.790 --> 10:11.280
No, Nishida-kun shouldn't know
 the details of Polka-kun's situation.

10:11.280 --> 10:13.750
The only bartender who does is...

10:13.750 --> 10:15.360
<i>You've gotta be kidding me.</i>

10:15.360 --> 10:18.720
<i>I know Polka-kun is a 
necromancer, but still.</i>

10:19.780 --> 10:22.300
<i>Why did I get called over here?!</i>

10:24.250 --> 10:25.150
<i>Don't tell me...</i>

10:25.810 --> 10:27.630
Your friend

10:28.610 --> 10:32.440
may have been caught up 
in something disastrous.

10:35.400 --> 10:39.290
You can— can— can— can see me— me?

10:39.290 --> 10:43.370
Please, t-t-tell him— h-him that

10:43.370 --> 10:48.830
some— somebody k-k-killed— killed m-m-me.

10:48.830 --> 10:51.320
Wh-What do you mean, disastrous?

10:51.320 --> 10:53.350
<i>Why is he reacting like this?</i>

10:53.350 --> 10:55.300
<i>What's going on here?</i>

11:03.110 --> 11:07.220
Clarissa, I have a followup 
report about Nishida-san.

11:07.220 --> 11:08.500
Yes?

11:11.050 --> 11:13.400
Clarissa, we have a slight problem.

11:13.400 --> 11:15.610
The police came by, I suppose.

11:16.250 --> 11:19.840
They wanted to confirm whether 
Nishida-kun worked here.

11:19.840 --> 11:20.920
Are you psychic?

11:20.920 --> 11:23.690
Huh? Did she get all that right?

11:23.690 --> 11:26.000
They're awfully good at this.

11:26.580 --> 11:30.080
Just like when it was Hosorogi-san's turn.

11:32.180 --> 11:33.250
Now,

11:35.820 --> 11:39.990
I hope I have better luck 
finding him this time.

11:42.440 --> 11:45.470
<i>"Open up and talk to him," huh?</i>

11:45.850 --> 11:49.880
<i>But what am I supposed to say 
to the fake Polka, and how?</i>

11:49.880 --> 11:53.890
<i>And what if Miss Sayo finds 
out what I really am, too?</i>

11:54.600 --> 11:56.990
A clan of assassins?

11:56.990 --> 11:59.150
What does that have to do with sharks?

11:59.780 --> 12:02.650
<i>On second thought,
 I don't need to worry about her.</i>

12:03.280 --> 12:04.180
<i>Hmm?</i>

12:04.900 --> 12:06.250
<i>The police?</i>

12:06.250 --> 12:10.580
<i>I got mixed up with Solitaire, 
so I'm in trouble if they're here about him.</i>

12:10.580 --> 12:15.290
Now then, let's use the Solitaire 
case to break the ice.

12:15.290 --> 12:19.760
If Takumi Kuruya is inside, 
this won't take long.

12:21.760 --> 12:24.720
I'm willing to bet he's in there.

12:24.720 --> 12:26.150
Cool it, okay?

12:26.150 --> 12:27.600
Come on. Make way.

12:27.600 --> 12:28.710
Uh-oh.

12:29.180 --> 12:30.640
Hold it.

12:30.640 --> 12:32.160
Who're you?

12:33.540 --> 12:34.140
<b>Inspector 
Tsubaki
 Iwanome</b>

12:34.140 --> 12:35.590
The local guys, huh?

12:35.590 --> 12:37.010
And you are...?

12:37.010 --> 12:40.570
We're on assignment from HQ.
 Kindly step aside.

12:40.570 --> 12:42.200
No can do.

12:42.200 --> 12:46.030
If you're on the Solitaire case, 
I'm one of the lead investigators.

12:46.030 --> 12:50.120
Nothing to do with Solitaire. 
Our orders come from the top.

12:51.160 --> 12:54.420
There was a nasty mugging last night.

12:54.420 --> 12:58.670
We got a tip that the perp is 
laying low in this building.

12:58.910 --> 13:03.040
He works in a bar near here, Youtoukorou.

13:03.670 --> 13:05.960
If you're in Community Safety, 
you must've heard of it.

13:09.810 --> 13:12.520
Oh, hey, the fun's already started.

13:13.640 --> 13:15.350
What is <i>he</i> doing here?

13:15.350 --> 13:17.240
See someone you know?

13:17.240 --> 13:21.820
The detective I mentioned yesterday. 
The one who crushed my gang.

13:22.370 --> 13:26.490
I should've known I couldn't plan for 
everything with only info from on high.

13:26.490 --> 13:28.470
Of course you couldn't.

13:28.470 --> 13:33.180
Even we Agakuras have messed up because 
our clients didn't tell us enough.

13:33.180 --> 13:36.040
I get a kick out of that 
sort of thing, though.

13:36.330 --> 13:39.250
I guess I'd better investigate privately.

13:39.250 --> 13:41.410
Got any handy connections?

13:41.410 --> 13:45.470
I used to have a skilled information 
specialist on my side,

13:45.970 --> 13:49.680
but my business rival in 
Shinjuku snapped him up.

13:49.860 --> 13:51.180
<b>DROP EVERYTHING</b>

13:51.950 --> 13:53.350
<b>DROP EVERYTHING 
 THE COPS ARE HERE</b>

13:53.350 --> 13:55.960
Shit! Those aren't local cops!

13:54.850 --> 13:56.810
<b><b>DROP EVERYTHING 
 THE COPS ARE HERE 
 SORRY, I DROPPED THE BALL. 
 JUST PLAY ALONG 
AND DO WHAT THEY SAY.</b></b>

13:57.770 --> 13:59.700
Huh? What's going on?

13:59.700 --> 14:01.230
Be right with you!

14:02.700 --> 14:04.110
We're police officers.

14:04.500 --> 14:06.030
Who's in charge here?

14:06.530 --> 14:10.200
I manage this fortune-telling establishment.

14:10.410 --> 14:13.100
We're about to launch a search 
of this whole building.

14:13.570 --> 14:16.080
Please vacate the premises now if possible.

14:16.520 --> 14:17.630
Recognize this man?

14:18.220 --> 14:20.570
He's a suspect in a mugging case.

14:20.570 --> 14:21.890
H-Hey!

14:21.890 --> 14:23.590
Huh? Me? Me?

14:23.590 --> 14:24.590
No.

14:24.590 --> 14:27.980
We've received information that 
he's hiding in this building.

14:27.980 --> 14:30.050
Please cooperate with our investigation.

14:30.260 --> 14:31.340
I understand.

14:31.340 --> 14:35.020
N-No way! I... I haven't done anything!

14:35.240 --> 14:37.720
<i>A mugger? Now, of all times?</i>

14:37.720 --> 14:40.630
<i>A mugger flees into a 
building Solitaire left?</i>

14:40.630 --> 14:44.500
<i>Is there a connection? I want to 
check the mugger's background.</i>

14:44.870 --> 14:49.210
Excuse me, would you mind showing 
me the mugger's photo, too?

14:49.210 --> 14:50.960
Do you work here?

14:50.960 --> 14:51.660
Yes!

14:51.660 --> 14:52.990
Huh?! Hey—

14:52.990 --> 14:54.490
<i>Polka. Polka.</i>

14:55.200 --> 14:58.980
<i>Can you use your magic to 
search the basement right now?</i>

14:59.290 --> 15:00.170
<i>Why?</i>

15:00.540 --> 15:02.130
<i>I have a bad feeling.</i>

15:02.480 --> 15:04.590
<i>This sequence of events reminds me</i>

15:04.590 --> 15:07.920
<i>of five years ago, right 
before I was murdered here.</i>

15:08.730 --> 15:11.610
<i>If my intuition is correct, 
something is down in—</i>

15:11.610 --> 15:12.760
<i>I found it.</i>

15:12.760 --> 15:13.720
<i>What?</i>

15:14.570 --> 15:15.680
<i>Our basement...</i>

15:16.140 --> 15:17.270
Looks like a body.

15:16.740 --> 15:19.850
<i>...has that guy, Nishida's, corpse in it.</i>

15:17.270 --> 15:17.920
He's dead.

15:17.920 --> 15:18.640
Dead.

15:18.640 --> 15:19.850
It's a dead body.

15:20.140 --> 15:21.180
<i>This is bad.</i>

15:21.180 --> 15:24.810
<i>If they find a body here,
 I'll be farther from peace than ever.</i>

15:25.040 --> 15:26.750
<i>So, that's their game.</i>

15:27.210 --> 15:30.890
<i>You're awfully cold when children 
or your friends aren't involved.</i>

15:33.450 --> 15:36.820
You're too kind to wield death.

15:36.820 --> 15:40.660
That's all the more reason 
to draw a clear line.

15:40.660 --> 15:46.170
Don't under- or overestimate 
how far your power can reach.

15:46.480 --> 15:50.630
Otherwise, you'll lose a great deal.

15:51.130 --> 15:53.560
<i>Yes. I won't deny it.</i>

15:54.430 --> 15:55.130
<i>But...</i>

15:55.130 --> 15:58.850
No. No. Not... Not me!

15:59.390 --> 16:00.920
<i>right now, I feel like</i>

16:02.200 --> 16:04.750
<i>my hands can stretch a little further.</i>

16:16.360 --> 16:17.670
Nothing's here.

16:19.610 --> 16:21.620
Looks like an empty room.

16:21.880 --> 16:24.380
I was sure he'd be hiding in here.

16:26.540 --> 16:27.640
What did you find?

16:27.640 --> 16:30.070
He wasn't in the basement, sir.

16:30.070 --> 16:31.280
I see.

16:30.090 --> 16:31.010
Huh?

16:31.870 --> 16:32.560
What?

16:32.560 --> 16:33.620
O-Oh, nothing.

16:33.620 --> 16:36.000
I just thought he might be upstairs, then.

16:36.000 --> 16:38.670
He could already have escaped, too.

16:38.670 --> 16:42.310
If he's not in this building,
we'll check the nearby security cams.

16:42.310 --> 16:43.610
R-Right.

16:46.090 --> 16:49.950
So, the big store at Sakuradamon 
has started stocking up.

16:50.400 --> 16:52.870
The Shinjuku market will turn volatile.

16:53.360 --> 16:56.810
This could affect the price of hitmen.

16:57.880 --> 16:59.040
The police?

16:59.410 --> 17:01.260
In the building where Polka is?

17:01.260 --> 17:05.580
<i>Uh-huh. Not local cops. Probably from HQ.</i>

17:07.290 --> 17:08.790
And what about Polka's group?

17:08.790 --> 17:10.500
They're outside.

17:10.500 --> 17:12.600
Good thing the rain let up!

17:12.600 --> 17:13.930
Scary, isn't it, darling?

17:13.930 --> 17:15.470
I guess so.

17:15.470 --> 17:18.430
<i>There's a secret passage 
under the basement floor?</i>

17:18.650 --> 17:22.100
<i>I found it when I searched the 
whole building a while ago.</i>

17:22.590 --> 17:25.140
<i>It seemed to connect to another building,</i>

17:25.520 --> 17:29.130
<i>but it hadn't been used
 recently so I didn't worry.</i>

17:29.890 --> 17:32.820
<i>Secret passages were pretty 
common in the Empire.</i>

17:33.570 --> 17:36.050
<i>But I've learned one thing from this:</i>

17:37.010 --> 17:40.240
<i>someone is trying to catch 
this building in a trap.</i>

17:40.900 --> 17:42.620
<i>They're either after us...</i>

17:42.620 --> 17:47.220
<i>Or the property owner, Clarissa.</i>

17:49.920 --> 17:53.410
Oh, I thought I'd find you here,

17:53.410 --> 17:55.050
Takumi Kuruya.

17:56.360 --> 17:58.070
Are you sure we shouldn't go over there?

17:58.070 --> 18:00.220
As much as I'd love to, yes.

18:00.530 --> 18:02.470
I mean, Kochou-chan is here.

18:02.470 --> 18:05.430
She's a reporter for
 <i>Weekly Dry</i> now, isn't she?

18:05.430 --> 18:08.650
She seems to be writing 
about Polka Shinoyama.

18:08.650 --> 18:13.400
It looks like they left quietly without 
a fight, so let's wait and see.

18:13.670 --> 18:17.110
I'm more worried about the guys 
in uniform the HQ team brought.

18:17.590 --> 18:19.270
Are they from Shinjuku Precinct?

18:21.240 --> 18:24.970
HQ coming out over a mugging 
stinks to begin with.

18:25.700 --> 18:30.640
Then they say one of Clarissa's 
bartenders robbed someone

18:30.640 --> 18:32.930
and fled to a building Clarissa owns?

18:33.340 --> 18:35.710
I'd like to know where that tip came from.

18:35.710 --> 18:37.670
You think it's fake info?

18:37.670 --> 18:39.510
The timing is too convenient.

18:39.850 --> 18:43.450
It's so perfect, I wouldn't be 
surprised if Solitaire set it up.

18:43.850 --> 18:46.230
Except that it's just like five years ago.

18:46.610 --> 18:48.390
After Hosorogi-san vanished,

18:48.390 --> 18:52.110
<b>From: Hosorogi
 To: Tsubaki Iwanome 

I found important evidence.
  It's at:</b>

18:48.810 --> 18:52.110
I got a text that said, 
"I found important evidence here."

18:54.780 --> 18:56.080
Hosorogi-san?

18:56.650 --> 18:59.510
When I came running, there was nothing there

18:59.910 --> 19:02.280
except for blood spatter on the walls

19:02.670 --> 19:05.270
that matched Hosorogi-san's DNA.

19:05.960 --> 19:07.230
I see.

19:08.080 --> 19:09.860
Kouzaburou Arase.

19:11.170 --> 19:13.500
If he's involved,

19:14.330 --> 19:17.870
I'll have to be more 
careful with my disguise.

19:18.290 --> 19:20.630
A hat won't be nearly enough.

19:21.610 --> 19:23.850
Momoya-san? What is it?

19:24.770 --> 19:27.810
I guess destiny is real.

19:28.250 --> 19:30.520
What the heck is going on?

19:34.850 --> 19:36.650
What are you doing here?

19:36.650 --> 19:37.890
Taipei.

19:37.890 --> 19:41.220
Your job is guarding Miss Sayo.

19:41.560 --> 19:44.120
I know. I'm already on my way back to her.

19:44.360 --> 19:48.460
You're no longer worth 
anything to the Lei family,

19:48.460 --> 19:53.250
but at least die doing your 
duty as her human shield.

19:53.250 --> 19:54.960
I don't need you to tell me that.

19:54.960 --> 19:57.700
I was done with the Leis ages ago,

19:58.320 --> 20:01.670
so don't presume to lecture me 
like you did back in the day.

20:01.670 --> 20:07.390
Are you sure? Without family 
ties, you're just a nobody.

20:08.520 --> 20:11.680
I think you'd better learn 
how to speak properly.

20:11.680 --> 20:13.780
Let go, Taipei.

20:14.400 --> 20:15.960
Yoo-hoo!

20:16.780 --> 20:18.570
S-Sakimiya-san!

20:18.570 --> 20:21.600
Are these groceries? I'll carry them for you!

20:21.600 --> 20:23.130
Oh, no, I can—

20:23.130 --> 20:25.580
Inside is kind of a mess right now.

20:25.580 --> 20:27.030
Huh? Umm...

20:29.910 --> 20:33.320
Way to go! New shark merch!

20:33.640 --> 20:36.340
I'm so glad you like them.

20:34.500 --> 20:39.050
Oh, I could never have too many of these!

20:37.960 --> 20:39.050
Please excuse me.

20:39.150 --> 20:42.010
<b>From: Big Sis 

Dear Little Brother, 
 Please don't say such sad things. 
Whatever Dad or the big lug say,
 I, at least, love, love, love, love, love you, 
and you're worth the world to me. 
To prove it, I'll empty out Taipei's bank account 
for talking down to you and deposit his money
 in your account, so don't give up your your big sis, 
okay? 

Your knight in shining armor, Imbi</b>

20:39.150 --> 20:42.010
<b>m 0 0 l 330 0 330 200 0 200</b>

20:53.090 --> 20:54.410
Do you need something?

20:55.690 --> 20:59.650
Don't worry. I'm on the Shinoyamas' side.

20:59.650 --> 21:04.730
But that doesn't mean you're 
on <i>Polka-kun's</i> side, does it?

21:07.810 --> 21:09.910
This <i>is</i> Shinjuku, you know?

21:09.910 --> 21:13.290
You never know who you'll run into here,
 so you'd better watch out.

21:14.730 --> 21:18.400
Why does her life force seem so faint?

21:19.250 --> 21:21.110
"You never know"?

21:21.720 --> 21:22.810
I see.

21:24.320 --> 21:26.780
This really is the underworld.

21:27.680 --> 21:29.930
Who's that girl?

21:30.150 --> 21:31.890
She's no amateur.

21:31.890 --> 21:34.810
I'd say she's killed at least ten people.

21:35.210 --> 21:39.110
She's probably one of Shinjuku's assassins.

21:39.110 --> 21:40.270
Well, now.

21:41.500 --> 21:43.480
Kouzaburou Arase.

21:43.790 --> 21:45.700
The Shinoyamas' heir.

21:45.970 --> 21:47.780
The Leis are here, as well.

21:48.990 --> 21:51.120
And so is Takumi Kuruya.

21:51.880 --> 21:54.080
He's the last person I expected to run into.

21:54.080 --> 21:58.050
Good. I figured this would be a boring job,

21:58.050 --> 22:03.280
but it's shaping up to be 
work I can <i>really</i> enjoy.
